<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — DayBook"
  description="DayBook's Privacy Policy. Detailed disclosures on local client-side storage, cookie usage, Google AdSense policies, and GDPR/CCPA data rights."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
  eyebrow="LEGAL &amp; COMPLIANCE"
  headline="Privacy Policy &amp; Data Practices"
  subtitle="We believe privacy is a fundamental right. Learn how DayBook handles data, uses cookies, and complies with advertising standards."
  activeNav="privacy"
  lastUpdated="November 17, 2026"
>
  <section>
    <div class="callout-box adsense">
      <h3 style="color:#cb009e;">Summary for Quick Reading</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Your notes and tasks are strictly private</strong>: They are saved directly inside your browser’s local storage on your device. We do not transmit or store your note text on any external servers. To keep DayBook free, we display third-party advertisements through <strong>Google AdSense</strong>, which uses cookies to show relevant ads. You can opt out of personalized advertising at any time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy applies to the <strong>DayBook</strong> web application available at <a href="https://daybook.com/">https://daybook.com/</a> ("DayBook", "we", "us", or "our"). This document explains our practices regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of information when you access our service, as well as your choices regarding data privacy.
    </p>
    <p>
      By using DayBook, you consent to the practices described in this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with these terms, please discontinue using the service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. User Content &amp; Local Client-Side Storage</h2>
    <p>
      DayBook is built with a <strong>local-first architecture</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No Server Transmission of Notes:</strong> The content of your notes, to-do lists, task priorities, and custom labels is stored exclusively within your web browser’s <code>localStorage</code> API.</li>
      <li><strong>No Account Required:</strong> You do not need to register, create an account, or provide personal credentials to use DayBook.</li>
      <li><strong>Data Ownership:</strong> You retain complete ownership of all content you create. DayBook has no technical ability to read, inspect, monetize, or decrypt your personal notes or checklist items.</li>
      <li><strong>Clearing Data:</strong> Because data is stored locally in your browser, clearing your browser’s cookies, cache, or site data will remove your local notes unless backed up.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Google AdSense &amp; Third-Party Advertising Policy</h2>
    <p>
      To provide DayBook as a 100% free service without paid subscriptions, we partner with third-party advertising networks, including <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. Google AdSense serves advertisements to users visiting our site.
    </p>

    <div class="callout-box adsense">
      <h3>Required Google AdSense &amp; Cookie Disclosures</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Third-Party Vendors and Cookies:</strong> Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites on the Internet.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising Cookies (including DoubleClick):</strong> Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to users based on their visits to DayBook and/or other websites across the Internet.</li>
        <li><strong>User Opt-Out of Personalized Ads:</strong> Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting Google's official Ad Settings page: <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.google.com/settings/ads</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Third-Party Network Opt-Out:</strong> Alternatively, users can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting the Network Advertising Initiative opt-out page at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aboutads.info</a> or <a href="https://youradchoices.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">youradchoices.com</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p>
      Third-party ad servers or ad networks use technologies like cookies, JavaScript, or Web Beacons in their respective advertisements and links that appear on DayBook, which are sent directly to users' browsers. They automatically receive your IP address when this occurs. These technologies are used to measure the effectiveness of their advertising campaigns and/or to personalize the advertising content that you see on websites that you visit.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em>Note: DayBook has no access to or control over these cookies that are used by third-party advertisers.</em>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small text files placed on your device to store data that can be recalled by a web server. DayBook and our third-party service partners use cookies and similar technologies for:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Essential Local Preferences:</strong> Storing your UI preferences (e.g., Light vs. Dark theme selection) in <code>localStorage</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics &amp; Performance:</strong> Anonymous traffic metrics via Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics (GTM-MWJR6JPC) to understand aggregate page views and performance trends.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising &amp; Targeting:</strong> Cookies placed by Google AdSense and its certified advertising partners to deliver and measure ads.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can choose to disable cookies through your individual browser options. Detailed information about cookie management with specific web browsers can be found at the browsers' respective websites.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. GDPR Compliance (European Economic Area)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a resident of the European Economic Area (EEA) or the United Kingdom (UK), you possess certain data protection rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR):
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The right to access, update, or delete:</strong> Since DayBook does not store personal accounts or note data on remote servers, your notes can be deleted at any time directly through your browser’s site settings.</li>
      <li><strong>The right of rectification:</strong> You can edit any note or task directly in the app.</li>
      <li><strong>The right to object &amp; restrict processing:</strong> You can opt out of personalized ad cookies using the links provided above.</li>
      <li><strong>The right to data portability:</strong> Your data remains client-side and can be copied directly from your local browser environment.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For any GDPR inquiries or questions, contact our data coordinator at <a href="mailto:work.sumritatiyagi@gmail.com">work.sumritatiyagi@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. CCPA / CPRA Compliance (California Residents)</h2>
    <p>
      Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), California residents have specific rights:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Right to Know:</strong> You may request information regarding the categories of personal data collected and shared.</li>
      <li><strong>Right to Delete:</strong> You can delete your locally stored data at any time by clearing your browser cache.</li>
      <li><strong>Do Not Sell My Personal Information:</strong> DayBook does not sell personal identifiable information. Third-party advertising partners may collect pseudonymous cookie identifiers for ad personalization; you can opt out via <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AboutAds.info</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Children's Online Privacy (COPPA)</h2>
    <p>
      Protecting the privacy of young children is especially important. DayBook does not knowingly collect any personally identifiable information from children under the age of 13. If you believe that your child has provided personal information on our website, please contact us immediately at <a href="mailto:work.sumritatiyagi@gmail.com">work.sumritatiyagi@gmail.com</a> and we will promptly remove such information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update our Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in our practices or applicable legal and regulatory requirements. Any updates will be posted on this page with an updated "Last Updated" date at the top. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Contact Information</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions, comments, or concerns about this Privacy Policy, our advertising practices, or data handling, please contact:
    </p>
    <div class="contact-card">
      <p style="margin:0 0 6px;"><strong>DayBook Privacy Team</strong></p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 6px;"><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:work.sumritatiyagi@gmail.com">work.sumritatiyagi@gmail.com</a></p>
      <p style="margin:0;"><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://daybook.com/">https://daybook.com/</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
